---
description: UI overlay, input and audio rules
globs: src/ui/**,src/input/**,src/audio/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- UI is plain TypeScript + HTML/CSS layered over the canvas (no React). Keep DOM updates out of the
  per-frame path: update HUD text at most 10x per second and only when the value changed.
- UI reads the `UiState` store from `src/shared` and sends `UiIntent`s (e.g. `host.setTeamSize`,
  `lobby.ready`). It never calls networking code directly.
- Host-only controls (team size, team assignment, mode, map, start) are shown only when
  `UiState.isHost` is true. Clients see the same panel read-only.
- Input produces one `InputFrame` per sim tick (type in `src/shared`). Support keyboard + mouse first,
  gamepad second. Pointer lock during matches; release it in menus.
- Key bindings live in one table so the settings menu can rebind them; store them in `localStorage`
  wrapped in try/catch.
- Audio: one shared `AudioContext`, resumed on the first user gesture. Cap simultaneous voices (see
  `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`). Positional sounds use cheap panning, not HRTF.
- Text and team colors must stay readable for color-blind players: teams are orange vs cyan and are
  also marked by icon shape.
